From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:11:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/34] surface_lazy: register a surface that leaves writes
 ahead; a second texture over the pages keeps it from doing so

A surface registered only as it left a standing, so writes left ahead by one
that had none could not be found by any reader. Two textures over one surface
learn of each other's writes from the copy back: neither leaves any ahead, and
a copy back recorded in an unordered encoder now reaches note_writes under the
new switches, where surface_lazy alone left it to the next resync.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
